-- CA_0243_record_2026_wisconsin_primary_results.sql
--
-- Slot CA_0243 reserved via `npm run steward --prefix backend -- slot CA` (author: Chris Andrews).
-- No migration runner exists; this file records SQL applied by hand.
--
-- Stale-primaries batch 3: record the outcome of every 2026-08-11 WISCONSIN Partisan Primary row that
-- still carried no result — Assembly (216 rows), State Senate (40), the statewide constitutional offices
-- (21: Governor, Lieutenant Governor, Attorney General, Secretary of State, State Treasurer) and two
-- Racine County offices (4). 281 rows, all written. Same shape as CA_0231 / CA_0237 / CA_0240: set
-- result, result_source, result_recorded_at; candidate_status is NOT touched.
--
--   won 234 · lost 47
--
-- Wisconsin prints EVERY party's primary for every partisan office, uncontested ones included, so every
-- row has a certified vote count — including single-candidate minor-party lines that won with a handful
-- of votes (e.g. AD10 Green, 4 votes). WEC's Canvass Results flag each of them "Winner"; recorded as won.
--
-- SOURCES (fetched 2026-09-24)
--   WEC  "2026 Partisan Primary Election Results" — "Official results ... certified on August 25, 2026":
--        County_by_County_Report_Partisan_Primary_2026_All_State_Contests.xlsx (645 party contests; every
--        contest total equals its candidate sum), the Canvass Results summary PDF (generated 2026-08-27;
--        its Winner flags agree with the xlsx for every row), and the Signed Canvass Statements (Chair
--        Don M. Millis, 2026-08-25) naming the statewide nominees. Every one of our 277 non-Racine names
--        was found in the xlsx.
--   Racine County (4 rows: Sheriff R — Madrigal 9,820 / Perez 5,605; Sheriff D and Clerk of Circuit
--        Court single candidates) — the county posts only its election-night report ("FINAL
--        UNOFFICIAL", 88/88 precincts) and no canvass. Its November 3 pre-election ZERO report
--        (2026-09-15) lists the same nominees on the general ballot, which settles who won (the NH
--        treatment in CA_0231); the counts are the unofficial ones and are labelled so.
--
-- NOTES
--   - Governor (D) was close: Crowley 315,413 / Hong 311,740 (0.46%). The signed canvass certifies
--     Crowley; no recount appears in the WEC record.
--   - Mandela Barnes (Governor D) is recorded 'lost' with his 32,435 certified votes: news reports he
--     suspended his campaign on 2026-07-30, but no official withdrawal exists and his name stayed on the
--     ballot.
--   - Our "Samuel Guerreo" (AD9 R) is "Sam Guerrero" in WEC — noted in result_source; not renamed here.
--
-- OUT OF SCOPE: Wisconsin's 32 U.S. Representative primary rows (Phase 167, Chris Cantrell — WI is one of
-- its clusters). Candidates on the canvass we have no row for (Governor D: Sara Rodriguez, Missy Hughes;
-- write-ins incl. AD3 D winner Michael J. Goodwin) are reported, not added.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT: every write is guarded on result IS NULL. Dry run: the body wrapped BEGIN; ... ROLLBACK;
-- against prod, applied twice in one transaction, then rolled back and re-read.
-- ROLLBACK (once applied): UPDATE essentials.race_candidates SET result = NULL, result_source = NULL,
--   result_recorded_at = NULL WHERE result_source LIKE '%Recorded by CA_0243 (2026-09-24).';

BEGIN;

CREATE TEMP TABLE ca0243_result ON COMMIT DROP AS
SELECT v.rc_id, v.full_name, v.status_before, v.result, v.result_source
FROM (VALUES
